WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.668
-All right, here we go.
"I got busted" -- here we go.

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:03.670
[ Laughs ]

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.371
This is from @AJDORRIS.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.474
He says, "I once wrote the
answers to a final on my hand.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:09.809
On the way out the door,
I made the mistake

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.177
of waving 'goodbye'
to my teacher."

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.245
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.947
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.784
This one's from @missmomogirl.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:20.687
She says,
"One time, I thew a party

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.854
when my parents were
out of town.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:22.989
I thought I was
in the clear

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.690
until my dad found
beer-can pyramids

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.392
in every single
kitchen cabinet."

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.460
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.595
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:29.996
That's what people do, man.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.697
-Yeah.
-Why?

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.365
Why would you do that? 'Cause
they wanted them to get busted?

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.368
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.036
What brats.
Come on, man.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.304
That's pretty funny.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.573
This one's from @KelHanna1.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:41.774
She says,
"I once asked my mom

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:43.843
to take a picture on my phone
for Instagram.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.845
After I'd been posing
for a while, she yelled,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.813
'Wow, honey.
51 people are watching!'

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:49.883
She'd accidentally started
a livestream."

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.785
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:58.992
How embarrassing.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.894
This one's from @vinekimber.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.530
She says, "I once forgot to do
an AP English assignment,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.099
so I hastily wrote down lyrics
to TV theme songs

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.667
and made them look
like poetry.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.770
Too bad my teacher
also watched 'Family Ties.'"

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.905
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:17.376
What would we do baby...
without us?

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.679
-Sha la la la.
-Sha la la la.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.782
This one's from @irishrose8.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.385
She says, "My friend and I snuck
into a bar when we were 17.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.620
The bartender brought over
drinks from someone at the bar.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.622
We turned to thank them,
and it was my dad."

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.256
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:32.992
Drink up,
'cause you're grounded.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.427
-You're grounded for life!

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.896
-[ Laughs ]
-The last thing you'll drink.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.197
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.900
That's a cool dad, though.
-What's he doing there?

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.002
-Yeah. What's he doing, man?
-Doesn't he have work to go to?

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.972
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.972 --> 00:01:47.973
-He has a night job,
do you think?

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.876
-Yeah.
I don't know, man.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.177
-Well, what do you think
he does for a living?

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.645
-I don't know.
He might, like...

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.047
make plastic spoons.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.181
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.683
You know what I mean?
Or, like, stuff...

00:01:57.683 --> 00:02:00.853
Like, work at Build-A-Bear,
stuff bears for a living.

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:03.255
-You assume that person's father
would either

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:05.191
make plastic spoons --
manufacturing --

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.693
or work at Build-A-Bear.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.295
-Yeah.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:13.132
Or make, like, comical mugs.
you know what I mean?

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.067
-Yeah. With funny sayings on it
and stuff like that,

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.803
handle on the wrong side.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.003
Ones with little things
on it, like,

00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:19.138
"Don't Start Without my Coffee."
-Yeah.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.906
-You know, stuff like that.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.109
Maybe. I don't know.
-Maybe.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.910
Either way, but Build-A-Bear,
you think that

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.712
more people would go
in the daytime...

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.013
-Yeah.
-...to get bears made.

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:29.482
-You'd think. But maybe night
is a great business.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.350
-There's a big night business.
-Yeah. Huge night business.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.452
-Huge night business...
-Yeah.

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:35.621
-...for making teddy bears.
-Yep.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:39.258
This one's from @devyy-d.
-Devyy-d.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.160
She says, "My friend
got tickets to 'Ellen,'

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.063
but my parents strictly told me
I wasn't allowed to go.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.231
I thought they've never
find out.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.367
They texted me this."
Look. There she is.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.803
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:54.239
"I see you, honey."
Wave to your parents.

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:55.642
[ Laughs ]

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:59.012
This one's from @ItsMeAshleyWee.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.314
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.348
-Who is it?

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.885
-It's me, Ashley Wee.
-Oh.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.587
She's a wee little girl.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.557
She says, "Driving home
after a job interview,

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.926
the car behind me started
honking the horn,

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.994
then cut me off.
I gave them the finger,

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.430
then realized it was the person
I had just interviewed with."

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.465
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.002
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.404
"You're hired.
No, you're not."

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.238
-This one is --
oh, this is funny --

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:29.042
from -- it's from @zombiederek.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.976
He says, "I accidentally
pocket-dialed a friend

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:33.045
while I was singing along
to songs on the radio

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.414
in Ray Romano's voice."

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.182
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.817
[ as Ray Romano ]
Debra!

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:38.851
Debra.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:44.490
♪ Find me in the club,
bottle full of bub ♪

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.959
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.761
[ Normal voice ] This one's from
@TheCookenMaster.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.964
She says,
"My parents got new iPhones,

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.365
and I got my mom's old one.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.966
I didn't realize everything
I did on my phone

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.434
got sent to her new phone.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.603
Every text.
Every picture."

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.372
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:03.208
-Ugh, yoinks.

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:06.479
-This last is form @SarahSpain
from ESPN.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.247
Hi, Sarah.
Thanks for playing the game.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.548
I love Sarah Spain.

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:12.451
She says, "I went on my first
date with my now-husband

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.620
to a Cubs/Cardinals day
at Wrigley Field.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.022
Boss saw us in the bleachers
on TV and texted me,

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.124
'How's the game, Ferris?'"

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.158
There you go.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.693
Those are our
"Tonight Show" hashtags.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.994
To check out more
of our favorites,

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.896 line:0%
go to tonightshow.com/hashtags.

